# Copy to the contest repository as .gitignore and add the contest's own entries.
# Fill in the secret and live-data sections BEFORE the first `git add -A`.

# tk.env and tools/toolkit/scripts/toolkit.env hold no secrets: commit them so every clone has the same settings.

# tk: local operation records (only at the repository root)
/runs/

# Legacy scripts: log-analysis output written where they run
/logs/

# Logs
*.log

# Secrets: settings with passwords and private keys. Do not ignore public keys the app needs.
# Examples (replace with the contest's own; check `git status --ignored` afterwards):
# /.env
# /env.sh
# *.key
# /private.pem

# Live data on the servers: list them before importing, and never let Git delete them.
# Examples (replace with the contest's own):
# /tenant_db/
# *.db
# /public/uploads/
